# ODPE Engine Architecture

## Overview

The Oscillating Dual-Process Echo (ODPE) engine evaluates every cognitive query through two geometric topologies simultaneously:

1. **Dodecahedron** (12 faces, 5 neighbors/face) — broad consensus evaluator with adjacency-based quorum validation.
2. **Deltoidal Icositetrahedron** (24 kite-shaped faces, 4 neighbors/face) — Catalan solid C_{24}, dual of the small rhombicuboctahedron. 26 vertices (8 cubic + 6 octahedral + 12 rhombicuboctahedral), 48 edges, face-transitive. Deep-resolution evaluator with adjacency-based quorum validation.

Both topologies apply consensus validation: outlier face scores are attenuated (0.5x) when fewer than 3 edge-neighbors agree within the divergence threshold (0.2). The resonance ratio between topology amplitudes classifies each query into a signal that governs context allocation, inference routing, memory recall, and C_emo modulation.

